  "//browserslist": "DB UX Design System v3 uses modern CSS such as light-dark(). Next.js processes CSS with LightningCSS, which downlevels light-dark() into a broken var(--lightningcss-light, ...) construct when the targets are old. Declaring targets that support light-dark() natively keeps the color tokens intact.",
